[0.003, "o", "\u001b[1;34mAgent Action\u001b[0m \u001b[34m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36mSummary: \u001b[0mfile_editor: {\"command\": \"create\", \"path\": \r\n\"/Users/alessioricco/certo-demo/projects/wordle/README.md\", \"file_text\": \"# Terminal Wordle\\n\\nA \r\nsmall Wordle game for the terminal, written in Python using only the standard library at \r\nruntime.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n- Python 3.10 or newer\\n- `pytest` to run the test suite\\n\\nCreate \r\nand activate a virtual environment, then install the test dependency:\\n\\n```bash\\npython -m venv \r\n.venv\\nsource .venv/bin/activate\\npython -m pip install pytest\\n```\\n\\nOn Windows PowerShell, \r\nactivate the environment with `.venv\\\\\\\\Scripts\\\\\\\\Activate.ps1` instead.\\n\\n## Play\\n\\nFrom the \r\nproject directory, run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython wordle.py\\n```\\n\\nThe game chooses"]
[0.000, "o", " a five-letter word and\r\ngives you six guesses. Enter exactly five letters for each guess. Each letter is reported as:\\n\\n- \r\n`correct`: the letter is in the right position;\\n- `present`: the letter is in the answer, but in \r\nanother position;\\n- `absent`: the letter is not available in the answer.\\n\\nInvalid-length guesses \r\ndo not use a turn. Press Ctrl-D (or Ctrl-Z then Enter on Windows) to end input, or Ctrl-C to quit; \r\nthe game exits with a goodbye message.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nRun the complete test suite \r\nwith:\\n\\n```bash\\npython -m pytest\\n```\\n\"}\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;34mAction:\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0mFileEditorAction\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;34mArguments:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m  command: \u001b[0m\"create\"\r\n\u001b[1m  path: \u001b[0m\"/Users/alessioricco/certo-demo/projects/wordle/README.md\"\r\n\u001b[1m  file_text: \u001b[0m\r\n    # Terminal Wordle\r\n    \r\n    A small Wordle game for the terminal, written in Python using only the standard library at \r\nruntime.\r\n    \r\n    ## Requirements\r\n    \r\n    - Python 3.10 or newer\r\n    - `pytest` to run the test suite\r\n    \r\n    Create and activate a"]
[0.000, "o", " virtual environment, then install the test dependency:\r\n    \r\n    ```bash\r\n    python -m venv .venv\r\n    source .venv/bin/activate\r\n    python -m pip install pytest\r\n    ```\r\n    \r\n    On Windows PowerShell, activate the environment with `.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\Activate.ps1` instead.\r\n    \r\n    ## Play\r\n    \r\n    From the project directory, run:\r\n    \r\n    ```bash\r\n    python wordle.py\r\n    ```\r\n    \r\n    The game chooses a five-letter word and gives you six guesses. Enter exactly five letters for \r\neach guess. Each letter is reported as:\r\n    \r\n    - `correct`: the letter is in the right position;\r\n    - `present`: the letter is in the answer, but in another position;\r\n    - `absent`: the letter is not available in the answer.\r\n    \r\n    Invalid-length guesses do not use a turn. Press Ctrl-D (or Ctrl-Z then Enter on Windows) to end \r\ninput, or Ctrl-C to quit; the game exits with a goodbye message.\r\n    \r\n    ## Tests\r\n    \r\n    Run the complete test suite with:\r\n    \r\n    ```bash\r\n    python -m pytest\r\n    ```\r\n  "]
